WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.041
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:07.076 --> 00:00:07.721
Dad?

00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:09.816
Sam. This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:11.904
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:14.168
Saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:14.203 --> 00:00:15.675
The family business.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.148
I got to find dad.

00:00:17.855 --> 00:00:20.078
I dreamt about Jessica's
death before it happened.

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:21.043
You got to be careful, all right?

00:00:21.078 --> 00:00:23.664
Ghosts are attracted to that
whole ESP thing you got going.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:26.080
I told you I don't have ESP.
I just have strange vibes.

00:00:26.115 --> 00:00:29.301
Weird dreams. Dead people
have weird dreams, man.

00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:32.487
I have these nightmares.
Sometimes they come true.

00:00:32.791 --> 00:00:34.087
Come again?

00:02:02.846 --> 00:02:05.236
Somebody help me! Somebody...!

00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:07.677
Somebody help...!

00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:39.183
Dean.

00:02:40.442 --> 00:02:41.711
Dean.

00:02:44.377 --> 00:02:46.938
What are you doing, man? It's
in the middle of the night.

00:02:47.156 --> 00:02:48.928
We have to go.

00:02:49.103 --> 00:02:51.185
What's happening? We have to go.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.718
Right now.

00:02:57.413 --> 00:02:58.295
Mcreedy.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.705
Detective Mcreedy. Badge number 158.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.121
I've got a signal four
eighty on progress.

00:03:03.156 --> 00:03:06.624
I need a registered
owner of a Two door Sedan.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:10.092
Michigan license plate
Mary, Frank, 6-0-3-7.

00:03:10.127 --> 00:03:11.569
Yeah, okay. Just hurry.

00:03:11.604 --> 00:03:12.973
Sammy, relax.

00:03:13.008 --> 00:03:16.258
I'm sure, its just a nightmare.
Yeah. Tell me about it.

00:03:16.293 --> 00:03:19.508
I mean it. You know, a normal
everyday naked class nightmare.

00:03:19.543 --> 00:03:21.859
This license plate, it
won't check out. You'll see.

00:03:21.894 --> 00:03:23.770
It felt different Dean. Real.

00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:26.226
Like we dreamt about our
old house and Jessica.

00:03:26.261 --> 00:03:29.112
Oh, yeah. That makes sense. Dreaming
about our house, your girlfriend.

00:03:29.147 --> 00:03:30.971
This guy in your dream,
you ever seen him before?

00:03:31.006 --> 00:03:32.503
No... No, exactly.

00:03:32.538 --> 00:03:35.187
Why would you have premonitions
about some random dude in Michigan?

00:03:35.222 --> 00:03:36.544
I don't know. Yeah, me neither.

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:37.975
Yes, I'm here.

00:03:41.643 --> 00:03:44.218
Jim Miller, Saginaw Michigan.

00:03:44.253 --> 00:03:46.794
You have the street address?

00:03:47.595 --> 00:03:49.950
Got it. Thanks.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.639
It checks out.

00:03:53.674 --> 00:03:55.268
How far are we?

00:03:56.259 --> 00:03:57.586
From Saginaw? Yeah.

00:03:57.621 --> 00:03:59.299
A couple of hours.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.903
Drive faster.

00:04:53.671 --> 00:04:55.159
What happened?

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.145
Suicide.

00:04:57.809 --> 00:05:00.522
I can't believe it.

00:05:02.477 --> 00:05:04.091
Did you know him?

00:05:04.126 --> 00:05:07.890
Saw him everyday at Saint Augustine.

00:05:07.925 --> 00:05:11.655
Always seems... seemed so normal.

00:05:11.831 --> 00:05:14.913
I guess you never know what's
going behind closed doors.

00:05:14.948 --> 00:05:17.607
I guess not. How did uh...

00:05:17.642 --> 00:05:20.232
What are they saying happened?

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.312
I heard they found him in the garage

00:05:22.347 --> 00:05:25.963
Locked inside his car
with the engine running.

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:28.944
Do you know about what
time they found him?

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:31.658
It just happened an hour or two ago.

00:05:31.693 --> 00:05:33.641
His poor family.

00:05:33.676 --> 00:05:37.450
I can't even imagine what
they're going through.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.329
Sam, we got here as fast as we could.

00:05:57.364 --> 00:05:59.455
Not fast enough.

00:06:00.085 --> 00:06:02.606
Which doesn't make any sense, man.

00:06:02.641 --> 00:06:04.657
Why would I even have these premonitions

00:06:04.692 --> 00:06:07.097
Unless there was a chance that
I can stop them from happening.

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:08.798
I don't know.

00:06:14.137 --> 00:06:16.674
So, what do you think killed him?

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.581
Maybe the guy killed himself.

00:06:18.616 --> 00:06:21.609
Maybe there's nothing
supernatural going on at all.

00:06:21.644 --> 00:06:24.324
I'm telling you. I watched it happen.

00:06:24.359 --> 00:06:27.004
He was murdered by something Dean.

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:29.059
It trapped him in the garage.

00:06:29.094 --> 00:06:30.864
Like what? A spirit?
A poltergeist? What?

00:06:30.899 --> 00:06:32.356
I don't know what it was.

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.585
I don't know why I'm
having these dreams.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.780
I don't know what the
hell is happening Dean.

00:06:37.055 --> 00:06:38.641
What?

00:06:38.676 --> 00:06:41.261
Nothing, man. I'm
just worried about you.

00:06:41.296 --> 00:06:43.367
Well, don't look at me like that.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.439
I'm not looking at you like anything.

00:06:45.663 --> 00:06:47.936
But I got to say. You look like crap.

00:06:47.971 --> 00:06:50.880
Nice, thanks. You welcome.

00:06:51.063 --> 00:06:53.855
Come on, let's just pick
this up in the morning.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.647
Check out the house,
we'll talk to the family.

00:06:57.107 --> 00:06:59.851
Dean, you saw them. They're devastated.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:02.595
They're not gonna want to talk to us.

00:07:04.017 --> 00:07:06.175
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:06.944 --> 00:07:09.505
But I think I know who they'll talk to.

00:07:10.579 --> 00:07:12.469
Who?

00:07:16.305 --> 00:07:19.270
This has got to be a
whole new loaf for us.

00:07:23.758 --> 00:07:25.440
Good afternoon.

00:07:25.475 --> 00:07:28.060
I'm Father Simmons.
This is Father Freely.

00:07:28.095 --> 00:07:30.646
We're new junior priests
at Saint Augustine.

00:07:30.681 --> 00:07:32.489
May we come in?

00:07:33.637 --> 00:07:35.056
Thanks.

00:07:35.653 --> 00:07:37.643
We're very sorry for your loss.

00:07:39.546 --> 00:07:43.300
In difficult times like these when the
Lord's guidance is most needed. Look...

00:07:43.335 --> 00:07:45.849
You want to pitch your whole
Lord has a plan thing fine.

00:07:45.884 --> 00:07:48.300
Don't pitch it to me. My brother's dead.

00:07:48.335 --> 00:07:50.886
Roger, please.

00:07:52.369 --> 00:07:54.313
Excuse me.

00:07:56.864 --> 00:08:00.029
I'm sorry about my brother in law.

00:08:00.064 --> 00:08:03.195
He's just so upset about Jim's death.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:04.875
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.583
That'll be great.

00:08:09.636 --> 00:08:12.638
It was wonderful of you to stop by.

00:08:12.673 --> 00:08:15.346
The support of the church
means so much right now.

00:08:15.381 --> 00:08:16.549
Of course.

00:08:16.584 --> 00:08:19.802
After all, we all are god's children.

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:28.412
What?

00:08:28.447 --> 00:08:32.519
Just tone it down a little bit, Father.

00:08:37.513 --> 00:08:39.149
So, Ms. Miller.

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:42.184
Did your husband have
a history of depression?

00:08:42.219 --> 00:08:44.001
Nothing like that.

00:08:44.036 --> 00:08:48.108
We... had our ups and
downs like everyone.

00:08:48.143 --> 00:08:50.554
But we were happy.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.734
I just don't understand

00:08:54.769 --> 00:08:58.240
How Jim could do something like that.

00:09:00.275 --> 00:09:03.924
I'm so sorry you had
to find him like that.

00:09:04.086 --> 00:09:06.314
Actually...

00:09:06.349 --> 00:09:08.542
Our son, Max.

00:09:09.019 --> 00:09:12.023
He was the one who found him.

00:09:12.058 --> 00:09:14.835
Do you mind if maybe...
I go talk to him?

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.029
No.

00:09:16.064 --> 00:09:18.273
Oh, thank you Father.

00:09:30.265 --> 00:09:31.578
Max?

00:09:31.613 --> 00:09:33.515
Hey, I'm Sam.

00:09:37.234 --> 00:09:40.191
Ms. Miller, you have a lovely home.

00:09:40.681 --> 00:09:43.726
How long have you lived here?

00:09:43.761 --> 00:09:46.771
We moved in about five years ago.

00:09:47.615 --> 00:09:50.442
You know, the only problem
with these old houses

00:09:50.477 --> 00:09:53.663
I bet you have all kinds of headaches.

00:09:53.698 --> 00:09:55.664
Like what?

00:09:55.699 --> 00:09:57.595
Well...

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.153
Weird leaks.

00:10:00.188 --> 00:10:02.327
Electrical shortages.

00:10:02.362 --> 00:10:06.289
Odd sort of noises at
night. That kind of things.

00:10:07.636 --> 00:10:10.435
No, nothing like that.

00:10:10.605 --> 00:10:12.870
It's been perfect.

00:10:18.768 --> 00:10:20.157
May I use your restroom?

00:10:20.192 --> 00:10:22.810
Oh, sure. It's just up the stairs.

00:10:22.845 --> 00:10:24.329
Okay.

00:10:27.498 --> 00:10:30.015
So, what was your dad like?

00:10:31.093 --> 00:10:33.361
Just a normal dad.

00:10:33.396 --> 00:10:34.813
Yeah.

00:10:34.848 --> 00:10:38.073
You live at home now?

00:10:38.108 --> 00:10:39.686
Yeah.

00:10:39.721 --> 00:10:43.530
I'm trying to save up
for school but it's hard.

00:10:50.885 --> 00:10:54.295
So, when you found your dad?

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.602
I woke up.

00:10:58.455 --> 00:11:01.282
I heard the engine running.

00:11:05.303 --> 00:11:08.244
I don't know why he did it.

00:11:11.588 --> 00:11:13.686
I know its ruff.

00:11:13.721 --> 00:11:15.750
Losing a parent.

00:11:15.785 --> 00:11:19.587
Especially when you don't
have all the answers.

00:12:14.659 --> 00:12:16.255
Anything?

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.895
Zip.

00:12:20.999 --> 00:12:23.583
Escanaba Motel No Vacancy

00:12:26.426 --> 00:12:28.738
So, what do you have? Well, nothing.

00:12:28.773 --> 00:12:31.601
Nothing bad has happened to the
Miller house since it was built.

00:12:31.636 --> 00:12:33.713
What about the land? No
graveyard, battlefields,

00:12:33.748 --> 00:12:38.786
Tribal lands or any other kind of
atrocity on or near the property.

00:12:39.517 --> 00:12:41.543
Hey, man. I told you. I
searched the house up and down.

00:12:41.578 --> 00:12:45.379
There were no cold spots,
no soul person, nada.

00:12:45.866 --> 00:12:47.853
And the family said
everything was normal.

00:12:47.888 --> 00:12:49.806
Well, if there was a
demon or poltergeist.

00:12:49.841 --> 00:12:51.639
You don't think somebody
would have notice something?

00:12:51.674 --> 00:12:54.756
I used the infrared thermo
scanner, man. There was nothing.

00:12:54.791 --> 00:12:57.243
So what? You think Jim
Miller killed himself?

00:12:57.278 --> 00:13:02.085
And my dream was some sort
of freakish coincidence?

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.654
I don't know.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:07.135
I'm pretty sure there's nothing
supernatural about that house.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:08.756
Yeah.

00:13:08.791 --> 00:13:10.342
Well...

00:13:11.017 --> 00:13:13.156
You know, maybe...

00:13:13.191 --> 00:13:15.470
Maybe there's nothing
to do with the house.

00:13:15.505 --> 00:13:17.717
Maybe it's just a...

00:13:17.752 --> 00:13:21.077
Gosh. Maybe it's connected to Jim.

00:13:21.112 --> 00:13:23.321
In some other way.

00:13:23.356 --> 00:13:25.531
What's wrong with you?

00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:28.640
My head!

00:13:28.675 --> 00:13:30.017
Sam?

00:13:31.645 --> 00:13:32.673
Hey!

00:13:32.899 --> 00:13:34.141
Hey!

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:36.521
What's going on? Talk to me.

00:15:16.604 --> 00:15:18.120
It's happening again!

00:15:18.155 --> 00:15:20.464
Something's gonna kill Roger Miller.

00:15:25.742 --> 00:15:27.522
Roger Miller?

00:15:28.179 --> 00:15:31.078
No, no, just the address please.

00:15:32.449 --> 00:15:34.310
Okay, thanks.

00:15:35.621 --> 00:15:39.765
450 West Grove. Apartment 1120.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.574
You okay?

00:15:41.823 --> 00:15:45.341
Yeah. If you're goon hurl. I'll
pull the car over, you know.

00:15:45.376 --> 00:15:47.788
I'm fine. Just drive.

00:15:47.823 --> 00:15:49.451
All right.

00:15:52.443 --> 00:15:53.969
Dean, I'm scared man.

00:15:54.004 --> 00:15:55.668
These nightmares weren't bad enough.

00:15:55.703 --> 00:15:57.333
Now I'm seeing things when I'm awake?

00:15:57.368 --> 00:15:58.758
And theses...

00:15:58.793 --> 00:16:04.997
Visions or whatever. They're
getting intense, painful.

00:16:05.032 --> 00:16:06.516
Come on man. You'll be all right.

00:16:06.551 --> 00:16:09.698
You'll be fine. What
is it about the Millers?

00:16:09.733 --> 00:16:14.856
Why am I connected to them?
Why am I watching them die?

00:16:15.074 --> 00:16:17.384
Why the hell is this happening
to me? I don't know Sam.

00:16:17.419 --> 00:16:19.401
But we'll figure it out, okay?

00:16:19.436 --> 00:16:22.469
We face the unexplainable every
single day. This is just another thing.

00:16:22.504 --> 00:16:25.012
No. It's never been us.

00:16:25.047 --> 00:16:27.637
It's never been in the family like this.

00:16:27.672 --> 00:16:31.314
Tell the truth. You can't tell
me this doesn't freak you out.

00:16:34.049 --> 00:16:36.333
This doesn't freak me out.

00:16:45.481 --> 00:16:46.795
Hey, Roger!

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.007
Hey, hold up a second.

00:16:48.042 --> 00:16:50.173
What are you guys,
missionaries? Leave me alone.

00:16:50.208 --> 00:16:51.727
Please!

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.605
Hey! Roger!

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.774
We're trying to help!
Please! Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:00.809 --> 00:17:02.526
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:02.797 --> 00:17:04.562
I don't want your help.

00:17:04.597 --> 00:17:06.282
We're not priests. You've
got to listen to us!

00:17:06.317 --> 00:17:08.618
Roger, you're in danger!

00:17:10.238 --> 00:17:11.710
Come on, come on.

00:18:16.041 --> 00:18:17.247
Here.

00:18:17.817 --> 00:18:19.043
Start wiping down your finger prints.

00:18:19.078 --> 00:18:20.166
We don't want the cops
to know we were here.

00:18:20.201 --> 00:18:22.076
Go! Go! Come on!

00:18:26.378 --> 00:18:28.352
I'm gonna take a look inside.

00:18:34.355 --> 00:18:35.981
I'm telling you there
was nothing in there.

00:18:36.016 --> 00:18:38.318
There's no signs either.
Just like the Miller's house.

00:18:38.353 --> 00:18:41.373
I saw something in the
vision. Like a dark shape.

00:18:41.408 --> 00:18:42.577
Something was...

00:18:42.612 --> 00:18:44.331
Something was stalking Roger.

00:18:44.366 --> 00:18:47.165
Well, whatever it was I'm sure
it's not connected to their house.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.362
No, it's connected to the family itself.

00:18:49.397 --> 00:18:51.835
So, what do you think?
Like a ventral spirit?

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.248
Oh, yeah. Few of them have been
known to ledge horn to families.

00:18:54.283 --> 00:18:55.856
They'll haunt them for years.

00:18:55.891 --> 00:18:58.642
Angier, Badges.

00:18:59.552 --> 00:19:01.022
Basically it was like a curse.

00:19:01.057 --> 00:19:03.658
Maybe Roger and Jim Miller got
involved in something heavy.

00:19:03.693 --> 00:19:06.837
Something curse worthy. And
now something's out for revenge.

00:19:06.872 --> 00:19:10.010
And they're making their family dying.

00:19:11.093 --> 00:19:13.845
Hey, you think Max is in danger?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.562
Let's figure out before he is.

00:19:16.597 --> 00:19:19.824
Well... I know one thing I have
in common with these people.

00:19:19.859 --> 00:19:21.546
What's that?

00:19:21.581 --> 00:19:23.963
Well, their families are cursed.

00:19:23.998 --> 00:19:25.946
Our family's not cursed.

00:19:25.981 --> 00:19:29.332
We're just had our dark spots.

00:19:30.442 --> 00:19:31.997
Our dark spots are...

00:19:32.032 --> 00:19:34.156
Pretty dark.

00:19:34.191 --> 00:19:36.280
You're dark.

00:19:39.704 --> 00:19:43.554
My mom's resting. She's
pretty packed. Of course.

00:19:43.916 --> 00:19:47.133
All these people kept
coming with like casseroles.

00:19:47.168 --> 00:19:49.719
I finally had to tell
them all to go away.

00:19:49.754 --> 00:19:54.223
You know, cause nothing says
I'm sorry like a tuna casserole.

00:20:06.515 --> 00:20:09.032
How are you holding up?

00:20:09.214 --> 00:20:10.877
I'm okay.

00:20:10.912 --> 00:20:14.296
Your dad and your uncle were close?

00:20:14.331 --> 00:20:17.121
Yeah, I guess. They were brothers.

00:20:17.156 --> 00:20:19.877
I use to hang out when I was little.

00:20:19.912 --> 00:20:24.153
But not lately, much?
No, it's not that. It's...

00:20:24.188 --> 00:20:26.599
We used to be neighbors
when I was a kid.

00:20:26.634 --> 00:20:28.976
We lived across town
in this house and...

00:20:29.011 --> 00:20:33.752
Uncle Roger lived next door so
he was over all the time. Right.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:39.026
So how was it in that
house when you were a kid?

00:20:39.061 --> 00:20:41.219
It was fine.

00:20:41.796 --> 00:20:43.141
Why?

00:20:43.176 --> 00:20:45.552
All good memories?

00:20:45.587 --> 00:20:48.351
You remember anything unusual?

00:20:48.386 --> 00:20:52.764
Something involving your
father and your uncle maybe?

00:20:53.951 --> 00:20:55.934
Why do you...?

00:20:56.108 --> 00:20:58.641
Why do you ask?

00:21:00.265 --> 00:21:02.712
It's just a question.

00:21:04.269 --> 00:21:08.561
No, there was nothing.
We were totally normal.

00:21:09.464 --> 00:21:12.433
Happy. Good.

00:21:13.303 --> 00:21:16.004
That's good.

00:21:16.645 --> 00:21:19.115
Well, you must be exhausted.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:21.586
We should take off. Right.

00:21:22.658 --> 00:21:26.065
Thanks. Yeah.

00:21:30.009 --> 00:21:32.360
Nobody's family is
totally normal and happy.

00:21:32.395 --> 00:21:34.712
You see when he was
talking about his old house?

00:21:34.747 --> 00:21:36.831
Sounded scared.

00:21:36.866 --> 00:21:38.768
Max isn't telling us everything.

00:21:38.803 --> 00:21:40.635
See we go find the old neighborhood?

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:43.391
Find out what life it
was with the Millers.

00:21:47.833 --> 00:21:49.673
Have you lived in the
neighborhood very long?

00:21:49.708 --> 00:21:51.331
Yeah, almost twenty years now.

00:21:51.366 --> 00:21:52.549
It's nice and quiet.

00:21:52.584 --> 00:21:53.698
Why you looking to buy?

00:21:53.733 --> 00:21:55.748
No, no, actually we
were just wondering if...

00:21:55.783 --> 00:21:59.548
If you might recall a family that use to
live right across the street I believe.

00:21:59.583 --> 00:22:01.954
Yeah, the Millers. They
had a little boy named Max.

00:22:01.989 --> 00:22:03.677
Right.

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:05.503
Yeah, I remember.

00:22:05.538 --> 00:22:08.471
Their brother had the place next door.

00:22:08.748 --> 00:22:10.909
So, what's this about?

00:22:10.944 --> 00:22:13.045
That poor kid okay?

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:15.146
What do you mean?

00:22:15.508 --> 00:22:18.618
Well, in my life. I've never
seen a child treated like that.

00:22:18.653 --> 00:22:19.952
I mean, I'd hear Mr. Miller

00:22:19.987 --> 00:22:23.372
Yelling and throwing things clear
across the street. He was a...

00:22:23.407 --> 00:22:25.116
Mean drunk.

00:22:25.151 --> 00:22:27.041
Used to beat the tire out of Max.

00:22:27.076 --> 00:22:30.829
Bruises. Broke his arm
two times that I know of.

00:22:30.864 --> 00:22:33.311
And this was going on regularly?

00:22:33.346 --> 00:22:35.107
Practically everyday.

00:22:35.142 --> 00:22:36.904
In fact that thug brother of his

00:22:36.939 --> 00:22:40.428
Was just as likely take a swing
at the boy. But the worst part...

00:22:40.463 --> 00:22:42.368
Was his step mother.

00:22:42.403 --> 00:22:44.585
She just...

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:47.966
Stand there, checked out. Never
lifted a finger to protect him.

00:22:48.001 --> 00:22:50.582
I must have called the
police seven or eight times.

00:22:50.617 --> 00:22:53.164
Never did any good. Now,
you said 'step mother'.

00:22:53.199 --> 00:22:56.223
I think his real mom
died. Some sort of...

00:22:56.258 --> 00:22:59.147
Accident. Car accident I think.

00:22:59.182 --> 00:23:01.348
Are you okay there?

00:23:03.131 --> 00:23:05.332
Uh, yeah. Thanks for your time.

00:23:05.367 --> 00:23:07.534
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Let's go.

00:23:08.596 --> 00:23:10.303
Oh, god.

00:23:21.919 --> 00:23:24.545
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:27.819
You know I didn't do
anything. That's right.

00:23:27.854 --> 00:23:31.357
You didn't do anything.

00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:35.719
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:38.263
How did you...?

00:23:40.998 --> 00:23:43.606
Max! Please!

00:23:55.585 --> 00:24:00.577
But every time you
stood there and watched.

00:24:00.612 --> 00:24:03.879
Pretending it wasn't happening.

00:24:03.914 --> 00:24:07.146
I'm sorry. No, you're not.

00:24:07.626 --> 00:24:10.680
You just don't want to die.

00:24:23.510 --> 00:24:25.380
Max is doing it.

00:24:25.415 --> 00:24:27.513
Everything I've been seeing.

00:24:27.548 --> 00:24:30.537
Are you sure about
this? Yeah, I saw him.

00:24:30.712 --> 00:24:32.130
How is he pulling it off?

00:24:32.165 --> 00:24:34.091
I don't know. Looks like telekinesis.

00:24:34.126 --> 00:24:35.982
So, he's Psychic? He's a spoon bender?

00:24:36.017 --> 00:24:38.646
I didn't even realize but
this whole time he was there.

00:24:38.681 --> 00:24:41.021
He was outside of the
garage when his dad died.

00:24:41.056 --> 00:24:43.362
He was in the apartment
when his uncle died.

00:24:43.397 --> 00:24:44.854
His visions this whole time.

00:24:44.889 --> 00:24:48.599
I wasn't connected to the
Millers. I was connecting to Max.

00:24:48.776 --> 00:24:51.554
The thing I don't know
is why man. I guess...

00:24:51.589 --> 00:24:53.402
Cause we are so alike?

00:24:53.437 --> 00:24:56.248
What are you talking about?
Dude's nothing like you.

00:24:56.283 --> 00:24:58.672
Oh, we both have psychic abilities.

00:24:58.707 --> 00:25:00.317
We're both... Both what?

00:25:00.352 --> 00:25:01.892
Sam, Max is a monster.

00:25:01.927 --> 00:25:03.886
He's already killed two people
now he's going for a third.

00:25:03.921 --> 00:25:06.607
With all he went through. The beatings.

00:25:06.642 --> 00:25:08.002
To want revenge on those people.

00:25:08.037 --> 00:25:10.663
I'm sorry man, I hate to
say it. It's not that insane.

00:25:10.698 --> 00:25:13.187
Yeah, but it doesn't justify
murdering your entire family.

00:25:13.222 --> 00:25:15.676
Dean... He's no different than
anything else we've hunted.

00:25:15.711 --> 00:25:17.624
All right, we've got to end it.

00:25:18.655 --> 00:25:20.771
We're not gonna kill Max.

00:25:20.806 --> 00:25:22.027
Then what?

00:25:22.062 --> 00:25:24.294
I hand him over to the cops
and say Lock him up, officer.

00:25:24.329 --> 00:25:26.727
He kills with his power
of his mind. Forget it.

00:25:26.762 --> 00:25:29.377
No way man. Sam! Do...

00:25:29.412 --> 00:25:31.173
He's a person.

00:25:31.208 --> 00:25:32.521
We can talk to him.

00:25:32.556 --> 00:25:36.273
Hey! Promise me you'll
follow my lead on this one.

00:25:37.163 --> 00:25:38.785
All right, fine.

00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:41.194
But I'm not letting
him hurt anyone else.

00:25:51.880 --> 00:25:55.838
You know I never did
anything. That's right.

00:25:55.873 --> 00:25:58.905
You didn't do anything.

00:25:59.182 --> 00:26:02.395
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:26:03.491 --> 00:26:05.369
Fathers?

00:26:07.496 --> 00:26:10.832
What are you doing here? Oh...

00:26:10.867 --> 00:26:12.620
Sorry to interrupt.

00:26:12.655 --> 00:26:14.339
Max, could we uh...

00:26:14.374 --> 00:26:18.513
Could we talk to you
outside for just one second?

00:26:19.660 --> 00:26:21.787
About what?

00:26:21.822 --> 00:26:23.705
It's... It's private.

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:26.516
Um... I wouldn't want to
bother your mother with it.

00:26:26.551 --> 00:26:29.526
We won't be long at
all though. I promise.

00:26:35.587 --> 00:26:37.028
Okay.

00:26:37.063 --> 00:26:38.469
Great.

00:27:04.617 --> 00:27:06.646
You're not priests!

00:27:12.745 --> 00:27:14.055
Max! What's happening?

00:27:14.090 --> 00:27:16.396
Shut up! What are you doing?

00:27:19.053 --> 00:27:21.343
I said shut up! Max, calm down.

00:27:21.378 --> 00:27:23.286
Who are you? We just
want to talk to you.

00:27:23.321 --> 00:27:25.195
Yeah, right. That's
why you brought this.

00:27:25.230 --> 00:27:26.889
That was a mistake, all right?

00:27:26.924 --> 00:27:29.151
So was lying about who we
were. But no more lying Max.

00:27:29.186 --> 00:27:30.980
Okay? Just please.

00:27:31.015 --> 00:27:34.262
Just hear me out. About what?

00:27:34.703 --> 00:27:37.347
I saw you do it.

00:27:37.382 --> 00:27:41.493
I saw you kill your dad and
your uncle before it happened.

00:27:41.528 --> 00:27:45.158
What? I'm having visions about you.

00:27:45.193 --> 00:27:47.050
You're crazy.

00:27:47.085 --> 00:27:49.342
So, you weren't gonna launch
a knife at your step mom?

00:27:49.377 --> 00:27:50.671
Right here?

00:27:50.706 --> 00:27:53.219
Isn't that hard to believe?
Max, look what you can do?

00:27:53.254 --> 00:27:56.130
Max, I was drawn here, all right?

00:27:56.707 --> 00:27:59.571
I think I'm here to help you.

00:28:02.443 --> 00:28:05.023
No one can help me.

00:28:05.058 --> 00:28:06.383
Let me try.

00:28:06.418 --> 00:28:07.830
We'll just talk.

00:28:07.865 --> 00:28:09.174
Me and you.

00:28:09.209 --> 00:28:13.438
We'll get Dean and Alice
out of here. No, no way.

00:28:14.151 --> 00:28:16.265
Nobody leaves this house!

00:28:16.300 --> 00:28:18.751
And nobody has to, all
right? They'll just...

00:28:18.786 --> 00:28:20.028
They'll just go upstairs.

00:28:20.063 --> 00:28:21.813
Sam, I'm not leaving you alone with him.

00:28:21.848 --> 00:28:23.461
Yes, you are.

00:28:23.496 --> 00:28:25.040
Look, Max...

00:28:25.075 --> 00:28:27.318
You're in charge here. All
right? We all know that.

00:28:27.353 --> 00:28:29.561
No one's gonna do anything
that you don't want to do.

00:28:29.596 --> 00:28:33.125
But I'm talking five
minutes here man. Sam...

00:28:35.742 --> 00:28:37.975
Five minutes?

00:28:39.053 --> 00:28:40.461
Go.

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:54.647
Come on.

00:28:59.276 --> 00:29:00.699
Look.

00:29:00.734 --> 00:29:03.300
I can't begin to understand
what you went through.

00:29:03.335 --> 00:29:05.942
That's right, you can't. Max...

00:29:05.977 --> 00:29:08.460
This has to stop. It will.

00:29:08.495 --> 00:29:10.943
After my step mother... No.

00:29:10.978 --> 00:29:12.928
You need to let her go.

00:29:12.963 --> 00:29:14.735
Why?

00:29:15.689 --> 00:29:17.643
Did she beat you?

00:29:17.678 --> 00:29:18.993
No.

00:29:19.028 --> 00:29:23.626
But she never tried to save
me. She's part of it too.

00:29:24.856 --> 00:29:26.587
Look what they did to you.

00:29:26.622 --> 00:29:30.516
Look what they all
did to you growing up.

00:29:30.551 --> 00:29:34.411
They deserve to be punished. Growing up?

00:29:34.446 --> 00:29:37.306
Try last week.

00:29:42.795 --> 00:29:44.812
My dad still hits me.

00:29:44.847 --> 00:29:48.347
Just in places people wouldn't see it.

00:29:49.348 --> 00:29:52.494
Old habits die hard I guess.

00:29:56.220 --> 00:29:58.154
I'm sorry.

00:30:03.618 --> 00:30:07.517
When I first found out
I could move things.

00:30:07.552 --> 00:30:09.856
It was a gift.

00:30:10.340 --> 00:30:14.060
My whole life I was helpless.

00:30:14.095 --> 00:30:16.663
But now I have this.

00:30:17.530 --> 00:30:19.833
So, last week...

00:30:19.868 --> 00:30:22.102
Dad gets drunk.

00:30:22.137 --> 00:30:24.585
First time in a long time.

00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:26.998
And he beats me to hell.

00:30:27.033 --> 00:30:29.774
It's the first time in a long time.

00:30:30.010 --> 00:30:32.725
And I do what I had to do.

00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:35.516
Why didn't you just leave?

00:30:35.551 --> 00:30:38.272
It isn't about getting away.

00:30:39.244 --> 00:30:43.368
Just knowing that they'd
still be out there.

00:30:43.651 --> 00:30:48.748
It was about not being afraid.

00:30:50.453 --> 00:30:53.236
When my dad used to look at me.

00:30:53.271 --> 00:30:55.984
There was hate in his eyes.

00:30:56.019 --> 00:30:59.561
Do you know what that feels like?

00:31:01.718 --> 00:31:02.981
No.

00:31:03.016 --> 00:31:06.109
He blamed me for everything.

00:31:06.144 --> 00:31:09.203
For his job. For his life.

00:31:09.238 --> 00:31:12.029
For my mom's death.

00:31:12.064 --> 00:31:15.376
Why did he blame you
for your mom's death?

00:31:17.998 --> 00:31:20.715
Because she died in my nursery.

00:31:20.750 --> 00:31:24.065
While I was asleep in my crib.

00:31:24.100 --> 00:31:27.381
As if that makes it my fault.

00:31:27.597 --> 00:31:29.645
She died in your nursery?

00:31:29.680 --> 00:31:30.889
Yeah.

00:31:30.924 --> 00:31:34.002
There was a fire and he get drunk

00:31:34.037 --> 00:31:38.102
And blab along like she
died in some insane way.

00:31:38.137 --> 00:31:40.529
He said that she burned up.

00:31:40.564 --> 00:31:43.395
Pinned to the ceiling.

00:31:48.517 --> 00:31:50.639
Listen to me Max.

00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:52.765
What your dad said.

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:55.504
About what happened to your mom.

00:31:56.451 --> 00:31:58.703
It's real.

00:31:59.857 --> 00:32:01.553
What?

00:32:01.588 --> 00:32:03.605
It happened to my mom too.

00:32:03.640 --> 00:32:05.561
Exactly the same.

00:32:05.596 --> 00:32:07.447
My nursery, my crib.

00:32:07.482 --> 00:32:10.253
My dad saw her in the ceiling.

00:32:10.794 --> 00:32:14.174
Your dad must have been
as drunk as mine. No.

00:32:14.209 --> 00:32:16.071
No, it's the same thing, Max.

00:32:16.106 --> 00:32:18.331
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:32:18.366 --> 00:32:20.676
That's impossible.

00:32:21.025 --> 00:32:24.617
This must be why I've been
having visions during the day.

00:32:24.791 --> 00:32:27.174
Why they're getting more intense.

00:32:27.366 --> 00:32:30.808
Cause you and I must be
connected in some way.

00:32:30.990 --> 00:32:33.846
Your abilities started six,
seven months ago, right?

00:32:33.881 --> 00:32:35.693
Out of the blue?

00:32:35.969 --> 00:32:37.044
How'd you know that?

00:32:37.079 --> 00:32:39.103
Because that's when my
abilities started Max.

00:32:39.138 --> 00:32:41.718
I mean, yours seem to be much
further along but still this...

00:32:41.753 --> 00:32:43.944
This means something. Right?

00:32:43.979 --> 00:32:48.904
I mean, for some reason.
You and I were chosen.

00:32:50.619 --> 00:32:52.790
For what?

00:32:53.654 --> 00:32:55.662
I don't know.

00:32:56.409 --> 00:32:58.614
But Dean and I... My brother and I...

00:32:58.649 --> 00:33:00.820
We're hunting for your mom's killer.

00:33:00.855 --> 00:33:02.503
We can find answers.

00:33:02.538 --> 00:33:05.114
Answers that can answer us both.

00:33:05.149 --> 00:33:07.691
But you got to let us go Max.

00:33:08.033 --> 00:33:11.326
You got to let your step mother go.

00:33:24.193 --> 00:33:26.137
No.

00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:29.487
What they did to me.

00:33:29.522 --> 00:33:32.299
I still have nightmares.

00:33:32.334 --> 00:33:35.063
I'm still scared all the time. Like...

00:33:35.098 --> 00:33:37.542
I'm waiting for that next beating.

00:33:37.577 --> 00:33:41.576
I'm just tired of being scared.
If I do this, it'll be all over.

00:33:41.611 --> 00:33:43.189
No, don't you get it?

00:33:43.224 --> 00:33:44.307
It won't.

00:33:44.342 --> 00:33:46.114
The nightmares won't end Max.

00:33:46.149 --> 00:33:47.959
Not like this.

00:33:47.994 --> 00:33:49.770
There's just...

00:33:49.931 --> 00:33:51.900
More pain.

00:33:52.143 --> 00:33:54.776
And it makes you as bad as them.

00:33:55.575 --> 00:33:57.655
Max...

00:33:58.242 --> 00:34:01.826
You don't have to go
this all by yourself.

00:34:06.741 --> 00:34:08.909
I'm sorry.

00:34:09.619 --> 00:34:11.064
No!

00:34:11.846 --> 00:34:13.446
Max!

00:34:15.277 --> 00:34:16.722
No!

00:34:16.757 --> 00:34:18.167
Max!

00:34:43.011 --> 00:34:44.373
Max!

00:34:46.588 --> 00:34:48.179
Son of a...

00:34:49.903 --> 00:34:51.275
Max.

00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:53.449
Max.

00:34:56.708 --> 00:34:58.243
No.

00:35:06.972 --> 00:35:08.567
Max.

00:35:10.087 --> 00:35:12.224
Stay back.

00:35:12.584 --> 00:35:14.418
It's not about you.

00:35:14.453 --> 00:35:17.512
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:35:18.849 --> 00:35:20.496
Okay.

00:35:38.894 --> 00:35:40.183
No!

00:35:40.915 --> 00:35:42.498
No!

00:35:54.155 --> 00:35:56.022
Max...

00:35:56.921 --> 00:35:58.632
No.

00:35:59.018 --> 00:36:01.134
Stay back.

00:36:01.332 --> 00:36:03.034
It's not about you.

00:36:03.069 --> 00:36:06.564
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:36:07.373 --> 00:36:09.241
Okay.

00:36:10.942 --> 00:36:13.473
No, don't! Don't!

00:36:13.508 --> 00:36:16.005
Please! Please Max!

00:36:17.107 --> 00:36:18.637
Max...

00:36:18.672 --> 00:36:21.051
We can help you.

00:36:21.264 --> 00:36:24.215
But this... What you're doing...

00:36:24.436 --> 00:36:26.552
It's not the solution.

00:36:26.587 --> 00:36:29.900
It's not gonna fix anything.

00:36:39.977 --> 00:36:42.509
You're right.

00:36:45.167 --> 00:36:46.692
No!

00:36:57.097 --> 00:36:59.319
Max attacked me.

00:36:59.354 --> 00:37:02.127
He threatened me with a gun.

00:37:02.830 --> 00:37:04.761
And these two?

00:37:06.714 --> 00:37:08.772
They're...

00:37:08.807 --> 00:37:11.231
Family friends.

00:37:12.279 --> 00:37:16.880
I called them as soon as
Max arrived. I was scared.

00:37:17.070 --> 00:37:19.588
They tried to stop him.

00:37:19.623 --> 00:37:22.107
They fought for the gun.

00:37:22.307 --> 00:37:25.169
Where did Max hid the gun?

00:37:27.011 --> 00:37:30.363
I don't know. He...

00:37:30.398 --> 00:37:33.715
Showed up and he...

00:37:37.153 --> 00:37:39.455
It's all right, Mrs. Miller.

00:37:40.905 --> 00:37:44.198
I lost everyone.

00:37:45.303 --> 00:37:46.903
Okay.

00:37:47.239 --> 00:37:49.326
We'll give you a call if we
have any further questions.

00:37:49.361 --> 00:37:51.124
Thanks officer.

00:37:51.576 --> 00:37:52.999
Come on.

00:38:05.667 --> 00:38:08.406
Freggis said something else.

00:38:08.441 --> 00:38:11.078
Got him through it
somehow. Don't do that.

00:38:11.113 --> 00:38:13.311
Do what? Told you yourself.

00:38:13.346 --> 00:38:16.189
It wouldn't matter what you
said. Max was too far gone.

00:38:16.224 --> 00:38:19.032
When I think about how he
looked at me man right before...

00:38:19.226 --> 00:38:20.564
I should have done something.

00:38:20.599 --> 00:38:22.783
Come on, man. You risked your life.

00:38:22.818 --> 00:38:26.225
I mean, yeah. If we gotten
there twenty years earlier...

00:38:28.126 --> 00:38:29.880
Well, I'll tell you one thing.

00:38:29.915 --> 00:38:32.051
We're lucky we had dad.

00:38:34.671 --> 00:38:38.228
I never thought you say that.

00:38:38.431 --> 00:38:39.705
Well...

00:38:39.740 --> 00:38:42.362
He could have gone away more after mom.

00:38:42.397 --> 00:38:47.893
A little more tequila a
little less demon hunting.

00:38:47.928 --> 00:38:51.360
Then we would have Max's childhood.

00:38:52.445 --> 00:38:54.855
All things considered.

00:38:54.890 --> 00:38:57.266
We turned out okay.

00:38:57.301 --> 00:38:59.616
Thanks to him.

00:39:03.317 --> 00:39:05.516
All things considered.

00:39:14.655 --> 00:39:15.911
Dean, I've been thinking.

00:39:15.946 --> 00:39:17.132
That's never a good thing.

00:39:17.167 --> 00:39:20.084
I'm serious. I've been thinking...

00:39:20.119 --> 00:39:23.828
Why would this demon or
whatever it is. Why would it...

00:39:23.863 --> 00:39:26.286
Kill mom and Jessica and Max's mother?

00:39:26.321 --> 00:39:27.909
You know, what does it want?

00:39:27.944 --> 00:39:30.143
No idea. Well, you think maybe...

00:39:30.178 --> 00:39:33.115
It was after us? After...

00:39:33.150 --> 00:39:35.957
Max and me? Why would you think that?

00:39:36.190 --> 00:39:37.464
I mean...

00:39:37.499 --> 00:39:39.462
Either telekinesis are premonitions.

00:39:39.497 --> 00:39:41.391
We both had abilities, you know.

00:39:41.426 --> 00:39:43.563
Maybe it was after us for some reason.

00:39:43.598 --> 00:39:46.712
Sam, if it wanted you. It
would have just taken you.

00:39:46.747 --> 00:39:47.898
Okay?

00:39:47.933 --> 00:39:49.510
This is not your fault.

00:39:49.545 --> 00:39:51.329
It is not about you.

00:39:51.364 --> 00:39:53.113
Then what is it about?

00:39:53.312 --> 00:39:55.789
It's about that damn thing
that did this to our family.

00:39:55.824 --> 00:39:58.572
That thing that we're gonna
find that thing we're gonna kill.

00:39:58.607 --> 00:40:00.718
And that's all.

00:40:01.997 --> 00:40:04.420
Actually, there's a...

00:40:04.455 --> 00:40:06.843
Something else too.

00:40:07.469 --> 00:40:08.846
Oh, geez what?

00:40:08.881 --> 00:40:12.084
When Max locked me in that closet.

00:40:12.119 --> 00:40:15.287
That big cabinet against the door.

00:40:15.639 --> 00:40:17.638
I moved it.

00:40:18.657 --> 00:40:21.516
Yeah, you're a little more up the body
strength than I gave you credit for.

00:40:21.551 --> 00:40:24.528
No man. I moved it. Like...

00:40:24.563 --> 00:40:26.664
Max.

00:40:29.408 --> 00:40:31.217
Oh.

00:40:33.136 --> 00:40:35.090
Right.

00:40:35.125 --> 00:40:37.044
Yeah.

00:40:43.733 --> 00:40:45.901
Bend this.

00:40:46.140 --> 00:40:47.812
I can't turn it on and off Dean.

00:40:47.847 --> 00:40:49.275
Then how'd you do it? I don't know.

00:40:49.310 --> 00:40:51.439
I can't control it. I just...

00:40:51.474 --> 00:40:55.011
I saw you die and it just came
out of me like a... Like a punch.

00:40:55.046 --> 00:40:56.327
You know, like a...

00:40:56.362 --> 00:40:59.133
Like a freak adrenaline thing.

00:41:02.776 --> 00:41:05.278
Well, I'm sure it won't happen again.

00:41:07.034 --> 00:41:08.766
Yeah, maybe.

00:41:08.801 --> 00:41:09.930
Aren't you worried man?

00:41:09.965 --> 00:41:12.643
Aren't you worried that I can
turn into Max or something?

00:41:12.678 --> 00:41:15.389
Nope. No way.

00:41:15.578 --> 00:41:16.773
You know why?

00:41:16.808 --> 00:41:18.459
No, why?

00:41:18.494 --> 00:41:20.730
Cause you got one advantage
that Max didn't have.

00:41:20.765 --> 00:41:22.483
Dad?

00:41:22.654 --> 00:41:24.892
Because dad's not here, Dean.

00:41:24.927 --> 00:41:26.570
No.

00:41:27.166 --> 00:41:29.248
Me.

00:41:30.397 --> 00:41:32.091
As long as I'm around...

00:41:32.126 --> 00:41:34.884
Nothing bad is gonna happen to you.

00:41:36.456 --> 00:41:38.153
Now then.

00:41:38.188 --> 00:41:41.026
I know what we need to
do with your premonitions.

00:41:41.061 --> 00:41:43.049
I know where we've got to go.

00:41:43.084 --> 00:41:45.099
Where?

00:41:45.330 --> 00:41:47.424
Vegas.

00:41:51.269 --> 00:41:53.588
What? Come on man.

00:41:53.785 --> 00:41:56.911
Craps table. We'd clean up.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.500
